<div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-12">
        <nav aria-label="breadcrumb">
            <ol class="breadcrumb">
                <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li>
                <li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/dms">DMS</a></li>
                <li class="breadcrumb-item active">Search</li>
            </ol>
        </nav>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Document Search and Retrieval</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Instant document discovery through powerful search capabilities combining full-text 
            indexing, metadata filtering, and intelligent relevance ranking across the entire repository.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Full-Text Search</h2>
        <p>
            OCR-indexed content enables searching within scanned documents as effectively as native 
            digital files. Full-text indexing processes document content during capture creating 
            searchable representations of text, spreadsheets, and presentation materials.
        </p>
        <p>
            Search results highlight matching terms within document previews allowing users to 
            assess relevance before opening files. Relevance ranking prioritizes documents where 
            search terms appear in titles, headings, or frequently throughout content.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Metadata and Advanced Filtering</h2>
        <p>
            Metadata filter search combines multiple criteria including date ranges, document types, 
            authors, departments, and custom fields. Complex queries locate documents created within 
            specific periods by particular authors containing specific content.
        </p>
        <p>
            Boolean search operators enable precise query construction using AND, OR, and NOT to 
            include or exclude terms. Phrase searching with quotation marks finds exact matches 
            while wildcard characters accommodate partial term matching.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Search Management</h2>
        <p>
            Saved search queries store frequently used criteria for one-click repetition. Users 
            create personal search libraries for recurring information needs such as monthly reports 
            or project-specific documents.
        </p>
        <p>
            Recent documents and favorites provide quick access to frequently referenced files 
            without repeated searching. The system learns from search patterns suggesting 
            relevant documents based on current work context and colleague activity.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-12 text-center">
        <p class="small mb-0">
            <a href="/dms" class="text-decoration-none">← Back to DMS</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
